peptide_wt4.dms.gz is an 8-residue helix (AEALKAIE) mapped to SIRAH beads with
SIRAH's own cgconv.pl, its topology built by GROMACS pdb2gmx -ff sirah, and
224 WT4 waters added by gmx solvate from the force field's own wt416.gro box:
930 beads with the parameters boonza read out of that topology.

The energies in tests/test_sirah.py are GROMACS 2024.6's for these very
coordinates, with PME converged (fourierspacing 0.08, ewald_rtol 1e-6) rather
than SIRAH's own mdp setting of 0.2, which leaves the reciprocal sum about
100 kJ/mol short on a system this size.

The SIRAH force field itself is not here: get it from https://www.sirahff.com.

crambin_cg.dms.gz is 1CRN (crambin) at pH 7 -- the .pqr of SIRAH's own
tutorial 3 -- mapped by cgconv.pl and built by pdb2gmx -ff sirah, without
solvent: 205 beads over 46 residues, with Ser, Thr, Tyr, Phe, Arg, Asp, Glu,
Asn and Cys, which is the chemistry the feature table is checked against.

1CRN_ph7.pdb is crambin with hydrogens at pH 7, the .pqr of SIRAH's tutorial
3 written as a PDB. sirahize maps it to the 205 beads of crambin_cg.dms.gz,
whose topology pdb2gmx -ff sirah built from the same beads: the counts and
energies in tests/test_sirah.py are that topology's.
